.TH YESH-LANGUAGE 7 "October 2026" "yesh" "Yesh Language Manual"
.SH NAME
yesh-language \- language reference for the yesh administrative shell
.SH PRINCIPLES
yesh has one preferred way to express a common operation. It keeps strings,
lists, regular expressions and command arguments distinct. It does not require
.B $,
historical test operators, or shell word-splitting rules.
.SH LEXICAL RULES
.IP \(bu 2
Indentation uses spaces; tabs are rejected.
.IP \(bu 2
Blank lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored.
.IP \(bu 2
Double-quoted strings use Go-style escapes.
.IP \(bu 2
Single-quoted strings preserve their contents and are recommended for regex.
.SH VALUES
.SS Scalars
.EX
name = web-1
message = "hello world"
.EE
.SS Lists
.EX
hosts = [web-1, web-2, web-3]
.EE
.PP
Nested lists are not supported in the current runtime.
.SS Regular expressions
.EX
unit = regex '^(api|worker)@[a-z0-9.-]+$'
.EE
.PP
The pattern is compiled when assigned. Invalid patterns and duplicate named
capture groups are errors.
.SH CONTROL FLOW
.SS if
.EX
if exists "/etc/myapp.conf":
    echo "configured"
else:
    echo "missing"
.EE
.PP
An external command can be used as a condition. Exit status zero selects the
body; a normal non-zero exit status selects
.B else.
Permission failures, symlink loops, signals and timeouts are execution errors,
not ordinary false conditions. Use only exists path; exists(path) is rejected.
.SS exit
.EX
exit 2
.EE
.PP
exit code terminates the entire script with an explicit decimal code from
0 to 255, including inside nested blocks. It is not a pipeline stage.
In plan mode exit is displayed without terminating plan traversal.
.SS matches
.EX
name = api-42
pattern = regex '^api-[0-9]+$'
if name matches pattern:
    echo "valid"
.EE
.SS for
.EX
for host in hosts:
    ssh host systemctl is-active api
.EE
.PP
Only finite lists are accepted. The runtime enforces iteration and total-step
limits. The
.B while
statement is disabled.
.SH COMMANDS
Commands remain Unix commands and are executed without an implicit shell.
Arguments are preserved as separate values.
.EX
grep error app.log | head 20
echo value > output.txt
cat < input.txt
.EE
.PP
The following constructs are rejected by default:
.B ; , & , && , || , $() ,
backticks, nested shell invocation, background jobs, and incomplete pipelines.
.SH ERRORS
Errors include the script filename and line number where available. A failed
external command stops normal execution. Missing executables and process
startup errors are not treated as ordinary false conditions.
.SH DESIGN BOUNDARY
yesh is an administrative scripting language, not a Python replacement and
not a Bash compatibility layer. SSH, rsync, systemctl, journalctl, mount and
other Unix tools remain external commands until a documented typed yesh
operation is added.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yesh (1)
